<article class="env-definition" id="01JZ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01JZ">Definition <span data-tag="01JZ">26.18.3</span>.</a> Properties and base change. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
Let $\mathcal{P}$ be a property of schemes over a base. We say that $\mathcal{P}$ is <em>preserved under arbitrary base change</em>, or simply that $\mathcal{P}$ is <em>preserved under base change</em> if whenever $X/S$ has $\mathcal{P}$, any base change $X_{S'}/S'$ has $\mathcal{P}$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Let $\mathcal{P}$ be a property of morphisms of schemes over a base. We say that $\mathcal{P}$ is <em>preserved under arbitrary base change</em>, or simply that <em>preserved under base change</em> if whenever $f : X \to Y$ over $S$ has $\mathcal{P}$, any base change $f' : X_{S'} \to Y_{S'}$ over $S'$ has $\mathcal{P}$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>